# Linux Learning Journey

## About This Repository

This repository documents my practical journey learning Linux fundamentals and cybersecurity.

I am a beginner, and my goal is to develop real technical skills through hands-on exercises, practice and consistent documentation.

## Practical 1: Ubuntu and WSL Setup

### What I worked on

- Explored Ubuntu running through Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL 2).
- Checked my current Linux user.
- Learned about the root account.
- Created a normal Linux user named `harrymofe`.
- Added the user to the `sudo` group.
- Configured Ubuntu to use my new account by default.

### Commands Practised

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `whoami` | Displays the current user |
| `pwd` | Displays the current directory |
| `uname -r` | Displays the Linux kernel release |
| `printenv WSL_DISTRO_NAME` | Displays the WSL distribution name |
| `ls /home` | Lists contents of the home directory |
| `getent passwd` | Displays account information |
| `id harrymofe` | Displays user and group information | 

